o your be in your office building  that's basically what they did  and now they're like wait a minute the  office buildings aren't there they're  not going to be as many people we've got  to refactor  our entire product strategy and our  sales strategy  to accommodate smaller environments and  working from home  so i believe that the way that people  will work  has changed forever so in 10 years it's  hard for me to predict  how much more it'll be different what i  do know is that  the the personalization that we've  achieved  by creating work environments that are  much more integrated i just told you my  kids will  come my dog already went by once right  it's got to get more personal  and we can't separate the work from the  home we can't separate  you know my identity as a mom and a wife  from my identity as  you know a vp or an executive or a ceo i  am  all those things and how we work and how  we create  the best work environments for people to  thrive in has to encompass  all those things i really see  independent contractors like i said  earlier they're not going  that that whole infrastructure is not  going anywhere  so i'm hoping that as we think about  developing new laws  at the federal and the state level those  laws will embrace  an economy that is ultimately here to  stay  you stacy and next we have irving  hi stacy thanks so much for speaking to  us today  my name is irving i'm an admitted  student to the gsb  my question for you is as you think back  to your time at stanford  what were some of the most valuable  lessons you took from the gsb that have  influenced your personal leadership  style  wow i i have so many so i'll do the like  touchy-feely one because you're all  wondering i'm sure  um i i i took i came  to stanford from a very  financial background i went to wharton  undergrad  i worked in public accounting and then i  worked in investment banking  so i really wanted to round out a lot of  my  analytical and finance skills and so i  took  marketing and organizational behavior  and all those classes  help me see that leadership is way more  than the spreadsheets  even though i was like a master at excel  like  i was really good i'm not good anymore  but i was really really good  some of the things that really helped me  is one just taking touchy-feely  like that class helped me see how other  people see me  and really understand the difference  between how you  show up and how other people see you i  can't think of  there's so many times as a manager where  people say well i tried to do this i  told them this  and i said well it doesn't really matter  what you said what matters is what they  heard and how they interpreted what you  said and i  learned that fundamental principle as  part of taking  taking touchy feeling so that's one of  the biggest things  thank you thanks cece i know i'm  really eager to take touchy feely i'm on  the waitlist so we'll see if i get in  next ring  so we have one last question for you  that we're asking all of our leaders  this year which is what principles do  you rely on when facing your toughest  moments as a leader  for me the absolute number one is  integrity  uh one of my favorite quotes which is  not  gender appropriate anymore but i'm going  to say it the way that he said it  is by dr martin luther king which is the  ultimate  measure of a man is not how he stands in  times of comfort and convenience but how  he stands in times  of challenge and controversy so we can  substitute the he  with she or they however but i want you  all to hear  how it was originally written and i  think about that  because that really calls into question  character  and when everything's fine we're all  fine but when everything's not fine  do you come with the sense of integrity  do you bring  the best person that you are to the  table  and that's really what guides me and  what i hope guides the people who decide  to work with me and for me  that's really inspiring i love that  quote i've never heard that before  um and i think we're all you know  walking away from this conversation  feeling motivated to bring our best  selves and our integrity  to work after seeing all that you've  accomplished and after seeing how you've  modeled such a wonderful career for so  many people  so thank you so much for being here  today it's been wonderful speaking with  you  thank you this was fun jessica thank you  so much  thanks stacy

